   $q$Read the sentence: "The new ferry is not only faster than the old one ___." Which choice keeps the sentence parallel?$q$, $q$[{"text":"and also quieter","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-correlative-pair"},{"text":"but it also runs more quietly","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"faulty-parallelism-correlative"},{"text":"but also it is quieter","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"faulty-parallelism-correlative"},{"text":"but also quieter","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$but also quieter$q$, $q$"Not only" is followed by the adjective "faster," so "but also" must be followed by a matching adjective, "quieter." The choices that add a subject and verb after "but" break the parallel pattern, and "and also" does not complete the "not only... but also" pair.$q$, 'draft', null)
