   $q$Read the sentences: "Our class visited the observatory. A white dome on the highest hill in the county." Which revision fixes the fragment?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Our class visited the observatory. Which is a white dome on the highest hill in the county.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-unfixed"},{"text":"Our class visited the observatory, it is a white dome on the highest hill in the county.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"Our class visited the observatory; a white dome on the highest hill in the county.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-phrase"},{"text":"Our class visited the observatory, a white dome on the highest hill in the county.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Our class visited the observatory, a white dome on the highest hill in the county.$q$, $q$"A white dome on the highest hill in the county" is an appositive that renames the observatory, so a comma attaches it correctly. A semicolon would need an independent clause after it, and this phrase has no verb.$q$, 'draft', null)
