   $q$Read the sentence: "The team tested the water samples then they compared the results with last year's data." Which revision fixes the run-on?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The team tested the water samples then, they compared the results with last year's data.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"The team tested the water samples, then they compared the results with last year's data.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"The team tested the water samples, and then they compared the results with last year's data.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The team tested the water samples, then, they compared the results with last year's data.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conjunctive-adverb-with-comma-only"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The team tested the water samples, and then they compared the results with last year's data.$q$, $q$Adding the coordinating conjunction "and" after the comma properly joins the two independent clauses. "Then" is an adverb, not a conjunction, so a comma before "then" still leaves a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
