   $q$The writer wants to add one more piece of evidence from Okafor's article to support the point in sentences 6 through 8. Which detail would be most relevant?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The busiest bus stop in Millbrook, used by about 900 riders a day, has no tree within a full block of it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Okafor's team bought its surface thermometers with a grant from the local university.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Okafor grew up in a coastal town where summers were cool and breezy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Many other cities around the world have also studied summer heat on their streets.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The busiest bus stop in Millbrook, used by about 900 riders a day, has no tree within a full block of it.$q$, $q$The paragraph argues that riders in unshaded areas face the most heat, and a busy stop with no nearby tree is direct, specific support for that point. The detail about other cities is too vague to show anything about Millbrook's shade.$q$, 'draft', '841f2565-2642-504f-afaa-fce168dbd8e2')
