   $q$Which sentence should replace sentence 2 to give the draft a clear, arguable claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Teenagers today should be allowed to work any job they want, just like the operators in Larkfield.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-analysis"},{"text":"Asante's article describes a telegraph office that opened in Larkfield during the year 1872.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"The telegraph was one of the most important inventions of the nineteenth century around the world.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-generalization"},{"text":"Asante's article shows that Larkfield's teenage telegraph operators held real responsibility and that the town depended on their skill.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Asante's article shows that Larkfield's teenage telegraph operators held real responsibility and that the town depended on their skill.$q$, $q$Both paragraphs give evidence that the young operators were skilled and trusted, so this claim matches the draft. The choice about the office opening in 1872 only restates a fact from sentence 1 and makes no point.$q$, 'draft', 'ca6d2cdb-7b02-594e-b9ce-ffad53a7f469')
