   $q$The writer first wrote sentence 7 as: The speaker is cold. "wearing the whole family at once." Why is the revised sentence 7 better?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It changes the poet's words slightly so that the quotation fits the writer's own style.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misquotes-source"},{"text":"It sets up the moment and blends the quotation into a complete sentence, so readers know who says it and when.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is shorter than the first version, and short sentences are always clearer for readers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"length-equals-strength"},{"text":"It moves the quotation to the start of the paragraph, where evidence should always appear.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-passage"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It sets up the moment and blends the quotation into a complete sentence, so readers know who says it and when.$q$, $q$The first version drops a quotation fragment in with no lead-in, while the revision gives context and integrates the words smoothly. The revision does not alter Kahale's words, and quoting accurately is required.$q$, 'draft', '5ed646ac-f522-5ec4-9ea2-1669a5d10f19')
