   $q$Which revision of sentence (8) most clearly links the objections to the writer's responses while keeping an objective tone?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both concerns are reasonable, yet each can be addressed with resources the city already has or has already planned.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Business owners complain about every change downtown, so their concerns carry little weight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismissive-tone"},{"text":"Cost and parking are important issues, and so are many other things in a city.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-wording"},{"text":"These concerns are serious enough that the project should probably wait several years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Both concerns are reasonable, yet each can be addressed with resources the city already has or has already planned.$q$, $q$The correct revision concedes that both concerns are fair and previews the answers in sentences (9) and (10), which makes the relationship clear. The choice about business owners dismisses opponents instead of answering them.$q$, 'draft', '1da3ac6d-cafc-54ab-b5b7-20736871f430')
