   $q$Which statement best evaluates the evidence in sentence (4) as support for sentence (3)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It weakens the argument, because it shows that performing makes students more anxious.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-evidence"},{"text":"It supports the confidence part of sentence (3), but it measures reported anxiety, not actual success in interviews or careers.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is irrelevant, because it studied university students rather than high school students.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-evidence"},{"text":"It proves that performing arts courses guarantee success in college and careers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It supports the confidence part of sentence (3), but it measures reported anxiety, not actual success in interviews or careers.$q$, $q$The study shows students reported less public speaking anxiety, which supports confidence but not proven career results. The study followed high school students, so calling it irrelevant misreads sentence (4).$q$, 'draft', 'd57fbe3c-2159-54a6-9e5b-b08e6e716cae')
