   $q$Which sentence about the essay contest is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Every eleventh-grade student who enters the essay contest which closes in March must submit a draft to a teacher.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"nonrestrictive-clause-not-set-off"},{"text":"Every eleventh-grade student who enters the essay contest, which closes in March, must submit a draft to a teacher.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Every eleventh grade student, who enters the essay contest, which closes in March, must submit a draft to a teacher.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restrictive-clause-set-off"},{"text":"Every eleventh-grade student, who enters the essay contest which closes in March, must submit a draft to a teacher.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"commas-around-wrong-clause"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Every eleventh-grade student who enters the essay contest, which closes in March, must submit a draft to a teacher.$q$, $q$"Eleventh-grade" is hyphenated as a modifier before "student"; "who enters the essay contest" identifies which students and so takes no commas, while "which closes in March" is extra information and is set off. Placing commas around the "who" clause would suggest every eleventh grader enters the contest.$q$, 'draft', null)
