   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 13 as the report's conclusion?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Pacers are the single most important reason runners finish marathons.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Next year, the writer plans to run a marathon with a four-hour pacer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"personal-shift"},{"text":"Used thoughtfully, pacers help runners apply the science of fuel and even effort, although each runner must still judge whether a group's pace fits that day.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Glycogen is a form of carbohydrate that muscles store for hard effort.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Used thoughtfully, pacers help runners apply the science of fuel and even effort, although each runner must still judge whether a group's pace fits that day.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion draws together the science in paragraph 2, the evidence in paragraph 3 and the caution in paragraph 4. Repeating the definition of glycogen only restates one detail.$q$, 'draft', 'c8218ee2-5998-5701-b8f6-f32e90dc055b')
