   $q$The writer wants to define a key term in sentence 7 without interrupting the explanation. Which revision does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"These acids also lower the dough's pH, a measure of how much the dough rises, creating conditions in which many unwanted microbes cannot survive.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inaccurate-definition"},{"text":"These acids also lower the dough's pH, which bakers in Westerby measure, creating conditions in which many unwanted microbes cannot survive.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-not-definition"},{"text":"These acids also lower the dough's pH (which is a really important science word), creating conditions in which many unwanted microbes cannot survive.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-non-definition"},{"text":"These acids also lower the dough's pH, a measure of how acidic a substance is, creating conditions in which many unwanted microbes cannot survive.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$These acids also lower the dough's pH, a measure of how acidic a substance is, creating conditions in which many unwanted microbes cannot survive.$q$, $q$The correct revision gives a brief, accurate definition that fits the sentence's point about acids. The choice defining pH as a measure of rising is wrong because rising comes from the yeasts' gas, as sentence 5 explains.$q$, 'draft', '3f1be365-dcb1-5bf7-8ba0-59cd8562079a')
