  ('e1e0b81c-e505-58ff-a8f3-b4369bce1ed5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-narrative-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which sentence, added after sentence 4, would best establish the narrator's point of view and the pressure of the situation?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mr. Pell had once worked at a larger store in another city before opening his own.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"focuses-on-wrong-character"},{"text":"Every time the cash drawer stuck, I could feel the line behind me growing more impatient.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Hardware stores often sell more supplies during storms than at any other time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact"},{"text":"The register was a newer model that Mr. Pell had bought two years earlier.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-without-stakes"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Every time the cash drawer stuck, I could feel the line behind me growing more impatient.$q$, $q$The correct choice puts the reader inside the narrator's nervous first shift alone. The register's age is a detail about the machine, not about how the narrator feels.$q$, 'draft', '0263af8c-9911-59cf-b483-df6aaced16f9')
