  ('c021fc9c-7a8b-52ef-8ca5-4502feed3906', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-narrative-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which sentence, added after sentence 18, would best conclude the narrative with reflection?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mr. Pell never did return the cracked shovel to the supplier after the storm.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ends-on-minor-detail"},{"text":"Ringing up that rake, I thought about Mr. Pell's tape and understood that he had sold Emeka a reason to come back.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The rake was on sale that week, so he saved a few dollars on his purchase.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"trivial-detail-ending"},{"text":"Spring is usually a busy season for hardware stores because people start working in their yards.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Ringing up that rake, I thought about Mr. Pell's tape and understood that he had sold Emeka a reason to come back.$q$, $q$The correct choice reflects on what Mr. Pell's small act of kindness accomplished, tying the ending to sentences 14 through 16. The sale price detail adds information but no meaning.$q$, 'draft', '0263af8c-9911-59cf-b483-df6aaced16f9')
