  ('5c17c9dd-0a40-5a96-a3ff-a801ff88a395', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-narrative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which revision of sentence 9 best builds tension by revealing the narrator's internal conflict?$q$, $q$[{"text":"I folded my chair, then unfolded it again, telling myself I would give the sky ten more minutes.","is_correct":true},{"text":"I almost went with them, and later I was glad that I had not.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reveals-outcome-early"},{"text":"Some of them were in my chemistry class, and we often studied together after school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"I almost went with them, but I did not, because I stayed on the hill instead.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"circular-no-conflict"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$I folded my chair, then unfolded it again, telling myself I would give the sky ten more minutes.$q$, $q$Folding and unfolding the chair shows the narrator torn between leaving and staying, and the deadline adds tension. "Later I was glad" gives away the outcome before the clouds part.$q$, 'draft', '889c5e8c-d2ae-54ab-bcb8-2938fb757d75')
