   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 16 as a conclusion that reflects on the experience?$q$, $q$[{"text":"After the lesson, we drove back home, parked the truck, and went inside to eat dinner.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"},{"text":"A manual transmission requires the driver to use a clutch pedal and shift gears by hand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"I still stall sometimes, but when I do, I hear her say \"Again\" and know it was never a scolding but an invitation.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It took me four afternoons in the empty lot behind the feed store to learn how to do it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-situation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$I still stall sometimes, but when I do, I hear her say "Again" and know it was never a scolding but an invitation.$q$, $q$The correct choice reflects on the meaning of the grandmother's repeated word from sentence 7. The choice about driving home lists actions but does not reflect on the experience.$q$, 'draft', '14f45f66-490f-575b-9b5b-685ec761fe27')
