  ('0fc92ad2-48ec-5628-9c27-d5d5efb88744', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-precise-language'), null, 'easy',
   $q$A student writes in a chemistry lab report: "The results were kind of off, so we redid the trial." Which revision best fits the formal style of a lab report?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The results were inaccurate, so the trial was abandoned.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"},{"text":"Because the results were inaccurate, the trial was repeated.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The results were way off, so we redid the whole thing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-word"},{"text":"The results were sort of inaccurate, so we redid it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-hedge"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because the results were inaccurate, the trial was repeated.$q$, $q$The correct revision replaces "kind of off" and "redid" with formal wording while keeping both facts. "Sort of inaccurate" still hedges in a casual way, and "abandoned" changes what the students actually did.$q$, 'draft', null)
