   $q$A student writes in a persuasive essay: "In my personal opinion, I think the observatory should extend its public hours." Which revision removes the redundant wording?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The observatory should extend its public hours.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The observatory might possibly perhaps extend its public hours.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wordy-hedging"},{"text":"In my opinion, I think the observatory should extend its public hours.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"redundancy-remains"},{"text":"Personally, in my opinion, the observatory should extend its public hours.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"redundancy-remains"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The observatory should extend its public hours.$q$, $q$An essay already presents the writer's view, so "in my personal opinion" and "I think" repeat the same idea and can go. "In my opinion, I think" still says the same thing twice.$q$, 'draft', null)
