   $q$Read the sentence: "The search team checked the stream bank, combed through the ferns, and dug beneath three fallen logs." Which sentence would follow it to create the strongest emphasis through a contrast in sentence length?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Even though they had looked in all of these places very carefully for a long time, nothing at all turned up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"loses-contrast"},{"text":"Nothing, in the end, after all of that effort, turned up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"awkward-interruption"},{"text":"Nothing turned up.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Nothing turned up, and the team kept looking, and the day went on.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stringy-and"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Nothing turned up.$q$, $q$After a long sentence listing three actions, a three-word sentence lands with force. The sentence beginning "Even though they had looked" says the same thing but is so long that the contrast disappears.$q$, 'draft', null)
