   $q$Read the sentence: "The new solar panels on the library roof generate electricity that is used to power the building's lights." Which revision is the most concise without losing information?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The new solar panels on the library roof generate electricity, and this electricity is used to power the building's lights.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wordier"},{"text":"The new solar panels on the library roof generate power that powers the lights of the building.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repetitive-word"},{"text":"The new solar panels on the library roof power the building's lights.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The new solar panels on the roof generate electricity.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The new solar panels on the library roof power the building's lights.$q$, $q$"Power the building's lights" already implies generating electricity, so the clause "that is used to" can be cut. "The new solar panels on the roof generate electricity" is shorter but drops the library and the lights.$q$, 'draft', null)
