   $q$Read the sentence: "It is important to note that the wetland filters runoff before it reaches the bay." Which revision is the most concise without losing meaning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Importantly, it is worth noting that the wetland filters runoff before it reaches the bay.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wordy-phrase"},{"text":"It should be noted that the wetland filters runoff before it reaches the bay.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wordy-phrase"},{"text":"The wetland filters runoff.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-detail"},{"text":"The wetland filters runoff before it reaches the bay.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The wetland filters runoff before it reaches the bay.$q$, $q$"It is important to note that" adds no information, so the sentence is stronger without it. "The wetland filters runoff" cuts too much and loses where the runoff goes.$q$, 'draft', null)
