  ('63908c42-125c-5cbe-b658-09d5b115657a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-precise-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The new transit line will reduce traffic, cleaner air, and commuters will save time." Which revision uses parallel structure to give the sentence clarity and rhythm?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The new transit line will reduce traffic, the air will be cleaner, and save commuters time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"faulty-parallelism"},{"text":"The new transit line will reduce traffic, improving air quality, and to save commuters time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mixed-forms"},{"text":"The new transit line will reduce traffic, improve air quality, and save commuters time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The new transit line will reduce traffic and cleaner air and commuters saving time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"faulty-parallelism"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The new transit line will reduce traffic, improve air quality, and save commuters time.$q$, $q$Each item now begins with a verb ("reduce," "improve," "save"), so the list reads evenly. "The air will be cleaner" is a full clause among verb phrases, which breaks the pattern.$q$, 'draft', null)
