   $q$Read the sentence: "The archivist looked at the fragile letter very carefully, checking every line for faded ink." Which verb would replace "looked at very carefully" most precisely?$q$, $q$[{"text":"saw","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-verb"},{"text":"scrutinized","is_correct":true},{"text":"skimmed","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning"},{"text":"glanced at","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$scrutinized$q$, $q$"Scrutinized" means examined closely and in detail, which matches checking every line. "Skimmed" names a specific way of reading, but it means reading quickly, not carefully.$q$, 'draft', null)
