   $q$Read the sentence from a debate evaluation: "Ayaan's argument was weak because it rested on a single small survey." Which word would replace "weak" most precisely in this formal context?$q$, $q$[{"text":"bad","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-adjective"},{"text":"tenuous","is_correct":true},{"text":"brief","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning"},{"text":"lame","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$tenuous$q$, $q$"Tenuous" means thinly supported, which describes an argument resting on one small survey. "Bad" is formal enough, but it does not say how the argument falls short.$q$, 'draft', null)
