   $q$A neutral historical report states: "In 1972, the owners of the textile mill ____ the riverside building and moved production to a newer site." Which word best completes the sentence while keeping an objective tone?$q$, $q$[{"text":"abandoned","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"negative-connotation"},{"text":"ditched","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-word"},{"text":"fled","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"loaded-verb"},{"text":"vacated","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$vacated$q$, $q$"Vacated" means left a building, with no judgment attached. "Abandoned" is formal, but it suggests neglect or desertion, which the report does not claim.$q$, 'draft', null)
