  ('55980990-62ee-5130-bcd9-a137117e6997', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-precise-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The desert plant known as the creosote bush is a plant that can survive for long periods of time without receiving any water." Which revision is the most concise while keeping all of the information?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The creosote bush survives without water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-detail"},{"text":"The desert plant creosote bush can live.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-detail"},{"text":"The creosote bush, a desert plant, can survive long periods without water.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The creosote bush is a plant that survives for long periods of time without any water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wordy-remains"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The creosote bush, a desert plant, can survive long periods without water.$q$, $q$The appositive keeps "desert plant," and "long periods without water" trims the filler. "Survives without water" is shorter but drops "long periods" and so overstates the claim.$q$, 'draft', null)
