   $q$Read the sentence: "The ice core samples arrived damaged, consequently the lab had to request a second shipment." Which revision of "damaged, consequently the lab" is correct?$q$, $q$[{"text":"damaged, and consequently; the lab","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-semicolon"},{"text":"damaged, consequently, the lab","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-with-conjunctive-adverb"},{"text":"damaged; consequently, the lab","is_correct":true},{"text":"damaged consequently the lab","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$damaged; consequently, the lab$q$, $q$"Consequently" is a conjunctive adverb, so the clauses need a semicolon before it and a comma after it. Adding a second comma around "consequently" still joins two independent clauses with only a comma.$q$, 'draft', null)
