   $q$Read the sentences: "The archive preserves fragile documents from the town's early years. Such as handwritten maps, ledgers from the first general store, and letters from settlers." Which revision of "years. Such as" fixes the fragment?$q$, $q$[{"text":"years, such as","is_correct":true},{"text":"years. Such as,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-unfixed"},{"text":"years: such as","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-with-such-as"},{"text":"years; such as","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-phrase"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$years, such as$q$, $q$"Such as handwritten maps..." is a phrase that gives examples, so it attaches to the main clause with a comma. A semicolon must be followed by an independent clause, which this phrase is not.$q$, 'draft', null)
