  ('b84e4a68-665e-541c-a5ce-2d6af8205665', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-sentence-structure'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The documentary follows a team of engineers as they designed a footbridge that floats on the river." Which revision keeps the verb tenses consistent?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The documentary followed a team of engineers as they design a footbridge that floated on the river.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tense-shift-moved"},{"text":"The documentary follows a team of engineers as they designed a footbridge that floated on the river.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tense-shift-unfixed"},{"text":"The documentary follows a team of engineers as they design a footbridge that floats on the river.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The documentary follows a team of engineers as they had designed a footbridge that floats on the river.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tense-shift-past-perfect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The documentary follows a team of engineers as they design a footbridge that floats on the river.$q$, $q$The engineers design the bridge during the events the documentary follows, so all three verbs stay in the present: "follows," "design," "floats." The "followed... design... floated" version moves the shift around instead of removing it.$q$, 'draft', null)
