  ('3e60dd47-6e9f-58f1-b967-a0749bd1c45a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-sentence-structure'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The report argued that the new transit line would reduce traffic, that it would lower emissions, and ___." Which choice completes the sentence with parallel structure?$q$, $q$[{"text":"it would create jobs for local workers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"faulty-parallelism-missing-that"},{"text":"creating jobs for local workers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"faulty-parallelism-gerund"},{"text":"that it would create jobs for local workers","is_correct":true},{"text":"the creation of jobs for local workers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"faulty-parallelism-noun-phrase"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$that it would create jobs for local workers$q$, $q$The first two items are both "that" clauses, so the third must also begin with "that." Without "that," the last item reads as a new independent clause instead of a third thing the report argued.$q$, 'draft', null)
