  ('fc9975bf-3ed4-5ab5-8574-24f60ac520ea', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-sentence-structure'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentence: "While still in high school, the city council invited Rafael to present his flood-mapping project." Which revision fixes the dangling modifier?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The city council, while still in high school, invited Rafael to present his flood-mapping project.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-modifier"},{"text":"While still in high school, an invitation came from the city council for Rafael to present his flood-mapping project.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-modifier-shifted"},{"text":"While still in high school, the city council invited Rafael, who presented his flood-mapping project.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-modifier-unfixed"},{"text":"While Rafael was still in high school, the city council invited him to present his flood-mapping project.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$While Rafael was still in high school, the city council invited him to present his flood-mapping project.$q$, $q$Turning the elliptical phrase into a full clause with "Rafael" as its subject makes clear who was in high school. Starting the main clause with "an invitation" still leaves the phrase describing something that cannot be in high school.$q$, 'draft', null)
